=== RULED OUT ===

Priority inversion.  7-minute run, 8898 fast samples, 0 slips: exactly ONE RT thread
  exceeded 0.3 ms runqueue WAIT in a window (pipewire/data-loop.0, 0.387 ms, before the
  load). Worst per-thread WAIT total across the load window: 0.84 ms over 7.5 s. Non-RT
  threads on the P-cores during the load: 1 (pipewire, pinned there deliberately).
Disk.  pgmajfault 0 throughout; psi_io 0 at the spike.
Clocks.  governor performance, C2/C3 disabled, P-cores 5.4-5.5 GHz across the window.
Graph rebuild.  Warm load (2nd Kontakt into the existing host, 472 ms, same graph work,
  no Wine startup) peaks at 0.431 ms. Sandbox "By Plugin" is per plugin type, not per
  instance, so the host is reused.
Minor-fault storm.  Wine host: 2,656,948 minor faults, 0 major, 602 MB anon during
  startup; system rate 6 k/s -> 621 k/s, correlating well at 1 s granularity. But a
  synthetic storm 7x larger moved data-loop.0 barely at all:
    quiet    (   ~6 k faults/s)  max 0.314  mean 0.255 ms
    storm A  (2.93 M faults/s)   max 0.521  mean 0.400 ms
    storm B  (4.46 M faults/s)   max 0.624  mean 0.502 ms   [18 GB/s clear_page]
  Contributory ~2x, not causal.
DXVK / lavapipe.  Kontakt imports dxgi.dll and OPENGL32.dll, so DXVK inits at DLL-load,
  enumerates every ICD and loads lavapipe with libLLVM.so.22.1 mapped twice (143 MB),
  then "Skipping: Software driver". Restricting VK_DRIVER_FILES and
  __EGL_VENDOR_LIBRARY_FILENAMES to the NVIDIA ICD: 0 LLVM mappings, VmSize 2.61 -> 2.28
  GB, min_flt 2,656,948 -> 2,657,210 (+262), Load MAX -0.024 ms. Lazily mapped file pages
  cost address space, not faults.

=== RESIDUAL ===

1.867 ms with no thread above 0.747 ms on-CPU. schedstat accounts for on-CPU and
runqueue-wait time only; a thread blocked on a futex is in neither, and Bitwig's Load is
wall-clock per callback. The peak lands in the same 20 ms window as "Engine loaded
plug-in", i.e. it is block time in the synchronous cross-process call at plugin
activation. Measuring it needs voluntary-context-switch counting, not schedstat.
